-      endpoints to determine the radiating direction exactly as in the base task family.
-    - Then each mover pixel disappears from its start cell and paints a 45-degree outward trail.
-      The diagonal keeps the wall opening's forward direction, while the side branch depends on
-      which side of the opening the mover starts on.
-    - If the mover begins at distance N from the wall sprite, it paints every Nth cell along that
-      diagonal, producing a sparse hop pattern instead of a solid ray.
